WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.963
Here's what you'll be able to
do by the end of this module.

2
00:00:02.963 --> 00:00:06.850
You'll name the three things
private-endpoint name resolution needs,

3
00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:08.350
and say where the zones live.

4
00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:11.481
You'll explain what a private
D N S zone group does,

5
00:00:11.481 --> 00:00:13.438
and how policy does it at scale.

6
00:00:13.438 --> 00:00:16.370
You'll prove a vault resolves
to a private address

7
00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:19.588
inside the network and
refuses requests from outside.

8
00:00:19.588 --> 00:00:22.124
You'll check a vault's role-based access,

9
00:00:22.124 --> 00:00:26.087
purge protection, firewall and
public access in one command.

10
00:00:26.087 --> 00:00:30.241
And you'll read the audit log for an
allowed and a denied secret read,

11
00:00:30.241 --> 00:00:33.262
and say why disabling a
suspected key comes last.

12
00:00:33.262 --> 00:00:39.503
You need Module 3; Migration C of the
service account guide, Service Accounts,

13
00:00:39.503 --> 00:00:45.150
from User Accounts to gMSAs to
Microsoft Entra Workload Identities,

14
00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:48.716
for the managed identities;
and a skim of D N S,

15
00:00:48.716 --> 00:00:52.940
D H C P and I P A M, which owns
the agency's D N S authority.
